maya: Proposal summary: default to gRPC+proto for internal S2S, maintain a managed gateway (Envoy/gRPC-transcoder or small auto-generated adapter) for browser/third-party JSON, provide codegen and CI hooks for proto evolution, and special-case streaming endpoints as gRPC-only.

chad: :thumbsup: if you agree, :confused: if you prefer REST everywhere, :eyes: if you want a follow-up RFC before deciding. I'll treat reactions as votes in 24h.

li: Also add: require tracing/span names in generated stubs (service.method) and include request size in metrics.

sophia: Add a lint rule in CI to block proto-breaking changes unless flagged and a migration plan is attached.

maya: Thanks — I'll draft a short RFC and a generator POC. Will ping infra for an Envoy config template.

oana: FYI, we'll need perf benchmarks (latency & p50/p95) for the gateway transcoder path vs direct gRPC so teams can see the cost.

sam: One more: SDK ergonomics matter. If we auto-generate idiomatic SDKs from protos, adoption will be easier.

maya: Cool — pulling together action items: 1) POC generator (li + maya), 2) Envoy gateway template (oana), 3) CI proto lint + dashboard wiring (sophia), 4) perf tests (chad/sam). I'll create the RFC draft later today.

